Docker
1. docker run mongo -> it will run a container for you locally (if not installed then it will install bydefault)
2. docker ps > will let you know the number of containers running locally
3. docker run -d mongo -> will let you run container but in a deattach environment so that my terminal will be free
3. docker run -p 27017:27017 -d -> will let you run a container using port mapping at deattached environment
4. docker kill id -> it will kill your container
5. docker rmi monog -> it will remove the image locally so that space could get free
6. How to create a dockerfile ?
	1. Create a Dockerfile inside the root dir
		FROM node:20
		WORKDIR /usr/src/app
		COPY package* .
		COPY ./prisma .
		RUN npm install
		RUN npx prisma generate
		COPY . .
		RUN npm run build
		EXPOSE 3000
		CMD ["node", "dist/index.js"]
	2. Create a .dockerignore (to make sure useless files should not go inside container)
		node modules
		dist
	3. TO build the container -> docker build -t my-app .
	4. Dont forget to save your files
	4. NOTE : Never pass your .env file into docker instead inject it
		eg: docker run -p 3000:3000 -e DATABASE_URL="..." my-app
7. How build an project from GitHub ?
	1. git clone the project
	2. docker build -t my-app .


* Whenever you will try to run a mongodb container and stores the data but if the container gets killed then all the stored data inside the mongodb compass will get deleted.
To avoid this - attach a volume to the mongodb container
1. docker volume create volume_database
2. docker run -v volume_database:/data/db -p 27017:27017 mongo
